    <div class="section-heading">EQUIPMENT (continued):</div>
    <div class="certificate-body">
        <p>Two <span data-field="equipment_type_1">{{ equipment_type_1 }}</span> are provided for the electrical connection on the side of the terminal head into the terminal compartment.</p>
        <p>Three tie rods in stainless steel (with aluminium guide boss) secures the terminal head to the front plate, in between which there is the body tube (squeezed between the terminal head and the front plate). The front plate contains a micro-gasket nitrile O-ring to provide an effective seal with the body tube; same being for the terminal head.</p>
        <p>A screw-on cover (lid) has a <span data-field="lid_dimension">{{ lid_dimension }}</span> internal threaded sections, which fits onto the terminal head. A groove accommodated nitrile O-ring is provided on the terminal head for an adequate sealing of the lid.</p>
        <p>Two glass lenses, approximately diameters <span data-field="lens_diameter">{{ lens_diameter }}</span> mm, are mounted in the front plate using nitrile O-rings. The lenses are kept in position onto the O-rings mounted from the inside of the enclosure with separate optical mountings (lens tubes) and screws. An option is provided for a heated lens so as to avoid condensation altering the optical characteristics.</p>
        <p>The device uses two individual lasers, one of which is used as a measuring laser (Class 1M) which produces an invisible infrared light. The other is used during installation and has a visible aiming laser (Class 3R) which is used to align the measuring laser.</p>
        <p>The model <span data-field="model_name">{{ model_name }}</span> is produced with heated lenses version option to accommodate different process needs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section-heading">Conditions of manufacture:</div>
    <div class="certificate-body">
        <p>The manufacturer shall comply with the following:</p>
        <ol style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.5;">
            <li>The resistance between the screw-on cover and front plate must be measured to ensure it is less than <span data-field="resistance_limit">{{ resistance_limit }}</span> $\Omega$.</li>
            <li>As required for insulated windings by IEC 60079-15:2010 Clause 23.2. 2, one of the following electric strength tests may be applied:
                <ul>
                    <li>Either 1800 V a.c. between the circuit and casing for at least 0.1 second (100 ms);</li>
                    <li>Or 2500 V a.c. r.m.s. between the circuit and casing for at least 60 second, alternatively, a d.c. test of 3000 V for 1 minute.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>No breakdown shall occur.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
